* fix(kanban): worker-terminal write refusal names the worker fence, not delegate_task [daveey] (#210)

A worker ran a board-repair script from its own terminal after two delegate_task
reviews, got 'delegate_task child contexts cannot mutate Kanban tasks or boards'
and filed a lineage-leak investigation (t_01a187533767dc4e). There was no leak:
scrub_kanban_env gives every tool subprocess of a worker the
HERMES_DELEGATED_CHILD_CONTEXT marker (owner = the worker's own pid) and drops
HERMES_KANBAN_TASK, with or without delegation; a fresh worker that never
delegated has the identical env. The DB-layer refusal named only delegate_task.

The env-inherited refusal now names the worker-terminal fence, the owning agent
pid and card, and the authorized paths (kanban_* tools, or board-repair code the
gateway/dispatcher runs). In-process delegate children keep their text; leaked
markers keep the leak diagnosis. Tests pin the parent terminal env as identical
before/after a delegate child and the refusal text per entry path.

* test(e2e): the dashboard concurrent writer commits at least 20 sessions however slow the box [daveey]

