* fix(kanban remote notices): the unloaded-chat sweep stops replaying stale and superseded cards [daveey] (#198)

* fix(kanban remote notices): the unloaded-chat sweep stops replaying stale and superseded cards [daveey]

Problem: 2026-10-29 00:22-00:36Z, right after the MacBook took 5bab4bb450, sweep_remote_notices
appended 293 "blocked" notices into ~216 idle chats for cards done days earlier (G1 t_cc5aeb02,
G6a t_414dafc6, G10b t_4bf9a311: "Held in ready by the respawn guard (active_pr) for 360 min", 10-24).

Why 1: the sweep read replica row default/t_cc5aeb02 (status blocked, run.ended_at 10-24) beside the
  current default/default/t_cc5aeb02 (done). The owner's hermes-hub client switched task keys from
  <board>/<id> to <profile>/<board>/<id>; the old rows stay frozen in the replica (hub copy today: 2,795
  ids with both shapes, newest legacy write 61 h ago).
Why 2: the sweep had none of collect()'s guards: no FRESH_S bound on the terminal time, no ledger check,
  and every replica row was read, so superseded rows counted as live state.
Why 3: 5bab4bb450 changed the blocked notice key to remote:<gw>:<key>:blocked@<ts>:<profile>:<sid>; no
  transcript held that key, so transcript-key dedupe (the sweep's only guard) let every stale blocked row
  through once per linked idle chat.
Root (happened): the poller and the sweep are two consumers of the same replica with separately coded
  admission rules; the freshness/identity rules lived only in collect().
Root (not caught): sweep tests seeded only fresh, canonical rows; none had an old terminal time, a
  legacy-key row, or a ledger row settled by collect().

Fix:
- _canonical(): one replica row per (owner gateway, task id), most qualified key then newest seq. Used by
  both collect()'s index and the sweep.
- The sweep announces only states that became terminal within FRESH_S (completed_at / run.ended_at, else
  completion_notice.created_at); older linked cards are counted and logged once per change.
- The sweep skips a notice the ledger already settled (acked, or recorded silently by collect(), e.g. a
  local placeholder covers it). Legacy pre-ack delivered=1 rows (no notice_key) are not trusted.

Tests (RED on origin/main, GREEN here): the three incident ids with legacy blocked rows beside done rows
append nothing; a 4-day-old blocked card appends nothing; a recent superseded legacy row yields only the
done notice from both sweep and poller in either row order; a ledger-settled notice is not swept; control:
fresh done + blocked notices are swept exactly once and acked, also after a restart.
Replay against the hub's real replica copy (gateway=macbook, fake store with no transcript dedupe):
origin/main 491 appends (155 blocked), this change 174 (17 blocked), all cards terminal within 6 h.

* fix(kanban remote notices): canonical rows drop only superseded legacy keys; collect uses the sweep's freshness clock [daveey]

