* fix(gateway): an agent adopting the gateway's bare session row records its model_config [daveey]

The gateway SessionStore creates a bare session row (model_config NULL) when a message
arrives. admit_durable_turn_lease then saw the row, set _session_db_created=True and so
skipped the agent's lazy create_session, which is the only writer of the agent's init
model_config (model_routing, max_iterations, reasoning_config, max_tokens). Gateway
(Slack) rows under `model.default: class:deep` therefore carried only gateway_runtime and
_usage_anchor, and stored_route resumed them as a concrete pin after a restart.

- SessionDB.seed_session_model_config fills only the keys a row lacks (existing keys,
  including explicit nulls, win), atomically.
- The lease calls it when it adopts a row this agent did not create.
- model_tools._resolve_active_context_length uses class_context_length for a class
  marker instead of probing the catalog with 'class:deep' (bogus warning + 256K fallback).

Tests: tests/gateway/test_class_row_provenance.py drives the gateway turn path
(TurnRunner._build_fresh_agent + run_conversation + _sync_session_model_from_agent) on a
bare row and asserts model_config.model_routing == the allocation store; fails before,
passes after. tests/tools/test_tool_search_context_provider.py covers the class gate.

* fix(desktop): a core-update restart is not a crash; exit cards dedupe and clear on reconnect [daveey]

hermes-sync's core update (`hermes update --yes`) SIGTERMs the Desktop-owned backend while it holds the
update marker. The exit supervisor sent `hermes:backend-exit` before its respawn path read that marker, so the
renderer raised the red "Hermes stopped working in the background" card (durationMs 0, fresh id each time)
four times on 2026-10-29 (07:29, 08:14, 08:38, 09:10), and nothing dismissed it once the respawned backend
was serving again.

- main: sendBackendExit classifies the exit (electron/backend-exit-report.ts) with the same predicate the
  skew checker uses (updateInFlight, update hand-off, live update marker); a planned one carries
  `planned: 'update'`. A probe failure reports unexpected, so a real crash is never hidden.
- renderer: a planned exit shows one quiet "Updating Hermes…" info notice post-boot and never fails the
  boot overlay; the crash card has a stable id so repeats replace it; the gateway socket's reopen dismisses
  both.

- code health: the sender lives in backend-exit-report.ts (main.ts shrinks); ja/ru/zh boot copy moves to
  ja_boot.ts/ru_boot.ts/zh_boot.ts like the other locales (unchanged strings plus the two new keys).

Tests: electron/backend-exit-report.test.ts (planned, unexpected, probe failure, sender: planned/unexpected/
soft re-home); use-gateway-boot-exit-notice.test.tsx (planned exit after boot, planned exit during boot, unexpected + repeated exits
keep one card, recovery clears the cards) - all four red on the previous hook.

