* fix(kanban): recover remote notices after offline gaps [daveey] (#214)

Owner timestamps reject notices arriving more than six hours late, and replica updated_at is server time. Persist a host baseline and immutable first-seen terminal times shared by both consumers. Seed all terminal history only from a complete synchronized snapshot; never give frozen legacy keys a local freshness window. Cache unchanged snapshots to avoid per-chat ledger transactions.

* perf(kanban): cold admission helper serves recorded plugin discovery and skill frontmatter [daveey] (#202)

* perf(kanban): cold admission helper serves recorded plugin discovery and skill frontmatter [daveey]

A fresh kanban admission helper under macOS background-tier I/O spent 24-44 s validating its
first card on the mini: provider discovery at hermes_cli.config import (5-10 s), loading all
plugins to learn whether terminal/file resolve (10-17 s), and re-parsing every SKILL.md for
frontmatter aliases (4-9 s). Each is now done once and reused by later cold processes, with
results identical to a fresh run:

- hermes_cli.config: the OPTIONAL_ENV_VARS additions (provider env vars, the core snapshot,
  platform manifest entries) run on first use, in the eager order, under a re-entrant lock;
  every dict method and the two derived frozensets trigger them.
- hermes_cli.plugins_snapshot: a discovery records its plugin toolset keys / portable MCP names
  with a stat-only fingerprint of its inputs and whether any plugin touched a built-in tool or
  toolset. _profile_capabilities serves that record (discovery suppressed) only when it is
  current, collision-free and grants every needed toolset; otherwise it runs the full discovery
  as before and records it.
- tools.skill_frontmatter_index: a cross-process, stat-revalidated index of SKILL.md parses
  under HERMES_HOME/cache, keyed by path + (dev, ino, size, mtime_ns, ctime_ns), stamped with
  the parser's code digest; only JSON-exact values; stock parser only.

* fix(kanban-cold): registry stages read the import-time home; failed stage retries; YAML loader rebinding bypasses the index [daveey]

Review of #202: a first OPTIONAL_ENV_VARS touch under another profile's home override read that
profile's provider/platform plugins process-wide (the eager import read the import-time home).
The stages now run under the home captured at install. A stage that raises leaves the registry
pending (as the failed eager import did) instead of half-built. The frontmatter index token now
covers the loaded YAML entry points, and a rebound yaml_load bypasses the index.

* fix(config): keep the import-time home initialization the eager provider discovery did [daveey]

Importing hermes_cli.config used to run load_config() inside provider discovery, so
ensure_hermes_home() secured the home once at import. With the env-var additions deferred,
the first ensure moved to the first config read and re-secured a home whose mode changed
after import (test_config_format_write_failure_is_owed_not_reported_complete: a 0555
profile home was reset to 0700, so the config write it must refuse succeeded).
config_env_registry.install(ensure_home=ensure_hermes_home) now runs it at import, logging
and dropping errors as the eager path swallowed them.
Test: test_importing_config_still_secures_the_home_once (red before, green after); the
lazy-registry test helper now carries the runner's sys.path to its child.

* test(kanban-cold): subprocess probes carry the runner's sys.path [daveey]

A runner that provides dependencies through PYTHONPATH (the hub's hermes env) lost them in
the probes' children (ModuleNotFoundError: ruamel); same remedy as
test_update_post_commit_safety._child_env.

* test(config): pin HERMES_HOME_MODE in the import-secures-home test so it holds on container CI runners [daveey]

The secure-dir policy skips an implicit chmod when it detects a container (CI runners are
detected as one), so the home stayed 0755 there. An explicit HERMES_HOME_MODE applies on
hosts and containers; the test still fails without the import-time ensure.

